The sale is 4 yogurts for $5.00. To find the number of sets of 4 yogurts in 60 yogurts:
$$
\frac{60}{4} = 15 \text{ sets}
$$

### Step 3: Calculate the total cost
Each set of 4 yogurts costs $5.00, so for 15 sets:
$$
15 \text{ sets} \times 5.00 \text{ dollars/set} = 75.00 \text{ dollars}
$$

