Each set costs $5.00, so 15 sets would cost 15 times 5. Let me do that multiplication. 15 * 5 is 75. So, $75.00?

Wait, let me double-check. Maybe I should check if there's any remainder when dividing 60 by 4. But 4 times 15 is exactly 60, so no remainder. That's good. So, no extra cost for any leftover yogurts. So, 15 sets at $5 each is indeed $75.

