The problem requires determining the difference in sleep duration between Harry and James. Harry slept 9 hours, while James slept $ \frac{2}{3} $ of that amount. 

**Step 1: Calculate how many hours James slept.**  
To find $ \frac{2}{3} $ of Harry's sleep time:  
$$
\text{James's sleep time} = \frac{2}{3} \times 9 = \frac{18}{3} = 6 \text{ hours}
$$

**Step 2: Calculate the difference in sleep time.**  
$$
\text{Difference} = \text{Harry's sleep time} - \text{James's sleep time} = 9 - 6 = 3 \text{ hours}
$$

